  "body": "`camcraft-motion` depends on `camcraft-sim`, so any change to a verify law rebuilds motion and its 65 test binaries. Split sim into the stock model (what motion needs) and `verify` above it; `Warning`, `crossed_pairs`, `crossing` and `RotaryAxis` get a home both sides can see.\n\nSafety floor: collision and gouge laws move files - no verdict may change; all sim and motion suites pass with the same test count.\n\nDone means: a change under `sim/src/verify` rebuilds no motion code; test counts and goldens unchanged. Do not start before #919 question 1 has timings that confirm the saving.\n\nLists, counts and evidence: the research comment on #919 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-6808141599).\n\nPart of #919.\n",
